{%- comment -%} Mirrors "The ritual is yours" (#steps) in site/index.html. Keep the copy identical to that file. {%- endcomment -%}
<section id="steps" aria-label="The method">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head head--idx"><div class="head-body">
      <h2 class="display">The ritual is yours. <em>The cycle is Sous.</em></h2>
    </div></div>
    <div class="steps steps--4" style="row-gap:44px">
      <div class="step"><span class="num">01</span><h3>Add water</h3><p>Pour water into the mixing cup before adding matcha. Use the etched 40, 80 or 120&nbsp;ml guide according to your preparation. For hot matcha, around 80&deg;C / 175&deg;F is a useful place to begin, though a particular tea may prefer something different.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><span class="num">02</span><h3>Sift matcha</h3><p>Measure your matcha and sift it directly over the water.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><span class="num">03</span><h3>Select + start</h3><p>Choose a saved setting, or customize one to your own speed and run time. Press start and let it run: it stops on its own when your matcha is ready.</p></div>
      <div class="step"><span class="num">04</span><h3>Serve + enjoy</h3><p>Serve it straight, build it over ice or finish it with milk. Rinse. Repeat.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="demo-note"><a class="textlink" href="/pages/how-it-works">See starting recipes &rarr;</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{ "name": "The ritual (steps)", "presets": [{ "name": "The ritual (steps)" }] }
{% endschema %}
